window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b105-7c6623825b2aa05f.json"]={sha256:"7c6623825b2aa05fa03b04052debc19ba4a5d24ef3af7cf7b8888c7fa19635d6",value:{"id":"b105","title":"切內里基線隧道","titleEn":"Ceneri Base Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"切內里是瑞士新阿爾卑斯鐵路線的南段關鍵，官方資料列長15.4公里並於2020年底全面營運。本課由縱坡與列車需求出發，連接施工物流、軌道基準、隧道氣動和設備交付；學員須解釋土建完成之後仍有哪些測試才能支持完整鐵路服務。","summaryEn":"Ceneri is a southern link of the Swiss new transalpine railway, officially described as 15.4 km and fully operational at the end of 2020. Starting with gradient and train demand, this course connects construction logistics, track reference systems, tunnel aerodynamics and equipment handover to the evidence needed beyond civil completion.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["坡度阻力功率","Grade-resistance power"],["有效掘進利用率","Effective boring utilisation"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","坡度阻力功率","有效掘進利用率","方向角誤差","所需疏散時間"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Grade-resistance power","Effective boring utilisation","Orientation error","Required evacuation time"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，再獨立計算「控制網與貫通誤差」。原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1436.5 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0463967 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate base-alignment grade and traction demand, then independently calculate control network and breakthrough error. Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1436.5 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0463967 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b105-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「基線縱坡與牽引需求」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b105-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將切內里基線孔與兩端接線分開，研究站間時間與隧道內行程不是同一計量邊界。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate the base bore from its approaches and distinguish station-to-station time from travel within the tunnel. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=13.6 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=13.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"將切內里基線孔與兩端接線分開，研究站間時間與隧道內行程不是同一計量邊界。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Separate the base bore from its approaches and distinguish station-to-station time from travel within the tunnel. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","將切內里基線孔與兩端接線分開，研究站間時間與隧道內行程不是同一計量邊界。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Separate the base bore from its approaches and distinguish station-to-station time from travel within the tunnel.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將切內里基線孔與兩端接線分開，研究站間時間與隧道內行程不是同一計量邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate the base bore from its approaches and distinguish station-to-station time from travel within the tunnel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b105-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=13.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=13.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.96 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=13.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.96 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=13.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=13.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.96 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=13.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.96 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：長度=13.6 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: length=13.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=13.6 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=13.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b105-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略站外接線會把隧道理論節時當成全線實際節時。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting approaches equates theoretical tunnel savings with whole-route savings. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較相同端點的路線和停站假設，保留接線速度限制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare equal endpoints and stopping assumptions while retaining approach speed restrictions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b105-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略站外接線會把隧道理論節時當成全線實際節時。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting approaches equates theoretical tunnel savings with whole-route savings. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略站外接線會把隧道理論節時當成全線實際節時。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Omitting approaches equates theoretical tunnel savings with whole-route savings. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略站外接線會把隧道理論節時當成全線實際節時。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitting approaches equates theoretical tunnel savings with whole-route savings.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略站外接線會把隧道理論節時當成全線實際節時。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting approaches equates theoretical tunnel savings with whole-route savings. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b105-v14-05","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以切內里低坡度路線連接區域與長途列車為題，分析相同坡度對不同質量列車的牽引需求。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use the low-gradient link to compare traction demand for regional and long-distance trains with different masses. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-05-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"以切內里低坡度路線連接區域與長途列車為題，分析相同坡度對不同質量列車的牽引需求。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Use the low-gradient link to compare traction demand for regional and long-distance trains with different masses. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","以切內里低坡度路線連接區域與長途列車為題，分析相同坡度對不同質量列車的牽引需求。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Use the low-gradient link to compare traction demand for regional and long-distance trains with different masses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以切內里低坡度路線連接區域與長途列車為題，分析相同坡度對不同質量列車的牽引需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use the low-gradient link to compare traction demand for regional and long-distance trains with different masses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b105-v14-06","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1436.5 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1436.5 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1436.5 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1305.91 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1436.5 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.28e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0052 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.28e+06 kg; grade=0.0052 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b105-v14-07","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：以空車質量估滿載運轉會低估坡度阻力，尤其混編比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using empty mass understates grade resistance in loaded and mixed formations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以同速同坡條件重算各列車質量的坡度分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recalculate the grade component for each mass at equal speed and slope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b105-v14-08","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以空車質量估滿載運轉會低估坡度阻力，尤其混編比較。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using empty mass understates grade resistance in loaded and mixed formations. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以空車質量估滿載運轉會低估坡度阻力，尤其混編比較。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Using empty mass understates grade resistance in loaded and mixed formations. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","以空車質量估滿載運轉會低估坡度阻力，尤其混編比較。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Using empty mass understates grade resistance in loaded and mixed formations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以空車質量估滿載運轉會低估坡度阻力，尤其混編比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using empty mass understates grade resistance in loaded and mixed formations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b105-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「破碎帶連通與預報更新」與「掘進利用率與設備停時」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" and \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b105-v14-09","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"切內里山區教學剖面保留節理方向改變，分析同岩性不同構造如何影響掌子面穩定與探查布置。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Retain changing joint orientation in a teaching section, examining how structure changes face behaviour even within the same rock type. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.2 無因次；通水面積=240 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.2 dimensionless; flow area=240 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-09-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"切內里山區教學剖面保留節理方向改變，分析同岩性不同構造如何影響掌子面穩定與探查布置。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Retain changing joint orientation in a teaching section, examining how structure changes face behaviour even within the same rock type. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["切內里山區教學剖面保留節理方向改變，分析同岩性不同構造如何影響掌子面穩定與探查布置。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Retain changing joint orientation in a teaching section, examining how structure changes face behaviour even within the same rock type.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"切內里山區教學剖面保留節理方向改變，分析同岩性不同構造如何影響掌子面穩定與探查布置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Retain changing joint orientation in a teaching section, examining how structure changes face behaviour even within the same rock type. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b105-v14-10","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.2 無因次；通水面積=240 m²。Q=k i A=0.00264 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.002904 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.2 dimensionless; flow area=240 m². Q=k i A=0.00264 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.002904 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.2 無因次；通水面積=240 m²。Q=k i A=0.00264 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.002904 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.2 dimensionless; flow area=240 m². Q=k i A=0.00264 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.002904 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.2 無因次；通水面積=240 m²。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.2 dimensionless; flow area=240 m².","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.2 無因次；通水面積=240 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.2 dimensionless; flow area=240 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b105-v14-11","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：同岩名即採同支護會漏掉新形成的可動節理塊體。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning support by rock name alone misses newly removable joint blocks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按方位而非只按岩名整理揭露資料，核對探孔代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Organise exposures by orientation as well as lithology and check probe representativeness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b105-v14-12","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同岩名即採同支護會漏掉新形成的可動節理塊體。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning support by rock name alone misses newly removable joint blocks. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同岩名即採同支護會漏掉新形成的可動節理塊體。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"Assigning support by rock name alone misses newly removable joint blocks. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同岩名即採同支護會漏掉新形成的可動節理塊體。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Assigning support by rock name alone misses newly removable joint blocks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同岩名即採同支護會漏掉新形成的可動節理塊體。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning support by rock name alone misses newly removable joint blocks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b105-v14-13","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比較切內里背景下的假想連續切削與循環開挖績效，將施工方法假設和正式工程史分開。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical continuous cutting and cyclic excavation in the Ceneri setting, clearly separating teaching methods from documented construction history. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.62 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.62 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-13-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"比較切內里背景下的假想連續切削與循環開挖績效，將施工方法假設和正式工程史分開。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Compare hypothetical continuous cutting and cyclic excavation in the Ceneri setting, clearly separating teaching methods from documented construction history. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","比較切內里背景下的假想連續切削與循環開挖績效，將施工方法假設和正式工程史分開。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Compare hypothetical continuous cutting and cyclic excavation in the Ceneri setting, clearly separating teaching methods from documented construction history.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較切內里背景下的假想連續切削與循環開挖績效，將施工方法假設和正式工程史分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare hypothetical continuous cutting and cyclic excavation in the Ceneri setting, clearly separating teaching methods from documented construction history. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b105-v14-14","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.62 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=11.4696 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.6166 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.62 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.4696 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.6166 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.62 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=11.4696 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.6166 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.62 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.4696 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.6166 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：切削速率=1.62 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.62 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.62 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.62 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b105-v14-15","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：只以最快切削分鐘比較兩方法會誤判整班生產能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing only the fastest cutting minutes misjudges whole-shift production. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對兩個假想班次使用相同總工時與完整停時分類。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use equal total shift time and complete downtime classes for both hypothetical shifts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b105-v14-16","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以最快切削分鐘比較兩方法會誤判整班生產能力。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing only the fastest cutting minutes misjudges whole-shift production. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以最快切削分鐘比較兩方法會誤判整班生產能力。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Comparing only the fastest cutting minutes misjudges whole-shift production. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只以最快切削分鐘比較兩方法會誤判整班生產能力。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Comparing only the fastest cutting minutes misjudges whole-shift production.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只以最快切削分鐘比較兩方法會誤判整班生產能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing only the fastest cutting minutes misjudges whole-shift production. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b105-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b105-v14-17","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙孔設備安裝同時進行時，軌道板、電纜與通風材料共用運輸通道，研究施工隊介面造成的等待。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During simultaneous twin-bore installation, track components, cables and ventilation materials share access and create inter-team queues. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=24 t；往返週期=34 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=24 t; cycle=34 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-17-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"雙孔設備安裝同時進行時，軌道板、電纜與通風材料共用運輸通道，研究施工隊介面造成的等待。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"During simultaneous twin-bore installation, track components, cables and ventilation materials share access and create inter-team queues. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","雙孔設備安裝同時進行時，軌道板、電纜與通風材料共用運輸通道，研究施工隊介面造成的等待。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","During simultaneous twin-bore installation, track components, cables and ventilation materials share access and create inter-team queues."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙孔設備安裝同時進行時，軌道板、電纜與通風材料共用運輸通道，研究施工隊介面造成的等待。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During simultaneous twin-bore installation, track components, cables and ventilation materials share access and create inter-team queues. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b105-v14-18","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=24 t；往返週期=34 min。C=N payload 60/T=169.412 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為154.011 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=24 t; cycle=34 min. C=N payload 60/T=169.412 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 154.011 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=24 t；往返週期=34 min。C=N payload 60/T=169.412 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為154.011 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=24 t; cycle=34 min. C=N payload 60/T=169.412 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 154.011 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=24 t；往返週期=34 min。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=24 t; cycle=34 min.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=24 t；往返週期=34 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=24 t; cycle=34 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b105-v14-19","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：材料到場被列為完成安裝會高估可用工作面和剩餘窗口。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating delivery as installation completion overstates available work fronts and remaining time. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按材料類別比較到場、卸載和實際安裝時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare arrival, unloading and installation times by material class. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b105-v14-20","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"材料到場被列為完成安裝會高估可用工作面和剩餘窗口。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating delivery as installation completion overstates available work fronts and remaining time. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"材料到場被列為完成安裝會高估可用工作面和剩餘窗口。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Treating delivery as installation completion overstates available work fronts and remaining time. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","材料到場被列為完成安裝會高估可用工作面和剩餘窗口。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Treating delivery as installation completion overstates available work fronts and remaining time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料到場被列為完成安裝會高估可用工作面和剩餘窗口。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating delivery as installation completion overstates available work fronts and remaining time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b105-v14-21","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"軌道與接觸網在切內里長孔內需共享幾何基準，分析土建控制點與軌道調整坐標之間的轉換。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Track and overhead systems need a shared geometric reference; examine transformations from civil control to adjusted railway coordinates. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-21-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"軌道與接觸網在切內里長孔內需共享幾何基準，分析土建控制點與軌道調整坐標之間的轉換。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Track and overhead systems need a shared geometric reference; examine transformations from civil control to adjusted railway coordinates. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["軌道與接觸網在切內里長孔內需共享幾何基準，分析土建控制點與軌道調整坐標之間的轉換。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Track and overhead systems need a shared geometric reference; examine transformations from civil control to adjusted railway coordinates.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軌道與接觸網在切內里長孔內需共享幾何基準，分析土建控制點與軌道調整坐標之間的轉換。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Track and overhead systems need a shared geometric reference; examine transformations from civil control to adjusted railway coordinates. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b105-v14-22","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0463967 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0463967 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0463967 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0463967 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3480 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3480 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0421788 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b105-v14-23","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：不同基準各自閉合仍可能使設備淨空在介面處不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Individually closed networks can still create inadequate interface clearance if their references differ. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"獨立核對軌頂高程、中心線和接觸網定位的版本。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently reconcile rail elevation, centreline and overhead positioning revisions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b105-v14-24","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同基準各自閉合仍可能使設備淨空在介面處不足。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Individually closed networks can still create inadequate interface clearance if their references differ. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同基準各自閉合仍可能使設備淨空在介面處不足。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Individually closed networks can still create inadequate interface clearance if their references differ. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["不同基準各自閉合仍可能使設備淨空在介面處不足。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Individually closed networks can still create inadequate interface clearance if their references differ.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同基準各自閉合仍可能使設備淨空在介面處不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Individually closed networks can still create inadequate interface clearance if their references differ. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b105-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「列車壓力波與動壓量級」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b105-v14-25","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車進出切內里孔口的壓力變化用來辨認氣動尺度，將動壓估算與實際壓力波幅及乘坐舒適分開。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use entry and exit pressure changes to distinguish dynamic-pressure scale from actual wave amplitude and passenger comfort. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=44 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=44 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-25-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"列車進出切內里孔口的壓力變化用來辨認氣動尺度，將動壓估算與實際壓力波幅及乘坐舒適分開。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Use entry and exit pressure changes to distinguish dynamic-pressure scale from actual wave amplitude and passenger comfort. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","列車進出切內里孔口的壓力變化用來辨認氣動尺度，將動壓估算與實際壓力波幅及乘坐舒適分開。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Use entry and exit pressure changes to distinguish dynamic-pressure scale from actual wave amplitude and passenger comfort.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車進出切內里孔口的壓力變化用來辨認氣動尺度，將動壓估算與實際壓力波幅及乘坐舒適分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use entry and exit pressure changes to distinguish dynamic-pressure scale from actual wave amplitude and passenger comfort. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b105-v14-26","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=44 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1405.54 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=44 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1405.54 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=44 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1405.54 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=44 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1405.54 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=44 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=44 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=44 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=44 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1161.6 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b105-v14-27","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：把動壓直接當洞口壓力波會忽略阻塞比與反射。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equating dynamic pressure with portal waves omits blockage and reflection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步對齊列車速度、位置和不同距離壓力訊號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise train speed, position and pressure signals at several distances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b105-v14-28","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把動壓直接當洞口壓力波會忽略阻塞比與反射。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equating dynamic pressure with portal waves omits blockage and reflection. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把動壓直接當洞口壓力波會忽略阻塞比與反射。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"Equating dynamic pressure with portal waves omits blockage and reflection. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把動壓直接當洞口壓力波會忽略阻塞比與反射。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Equating dynamic pressure with portal waves omits blockage and reflection.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把動壓直接當洞口壓力波會忽略阻塞比與反射。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equating dynamic pressure with portal waves omits blockage and reflection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b105-v14-29","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙孔鐵路的撤離先要辨認事故孔與安全孔狀態，行走距離只是通行能力和資訊延遲的一部分。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Twin-bore railway evacuation first identifies incident and safe-bore states; walking distance is only part of accessibility and information delay. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=88 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=88 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-29-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"雙孔鐵路的撤離先要辨認事故孔與安全孔狀態，行走距離只是通行能力和資訊延遲的一部分。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Twin-bore railway evacuation first identifies incident and safe-bore states; walking distance is only part of accessibility and information delay. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","雙孔鐵路的撤離先要辨認事故孔與安全孔狀態，行走距離只是通行能力和資訊延遲的一部分。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Twin-bore railway evacuation first identifies incident and safe-bore states; walking distance is only part of accessibility and information delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙孔鐵路的撤離先要辨認事故孔與安全孔狀態，行走距離只是通行能力和資訊延遲的一部分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Twin-bore railway evacuation first identifies incident and safe-bore states; walking distance is only part of accessibility and information delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b105-v14-30","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=88 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=513 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為555.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=88 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=513 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 555.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=88 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=513 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為555.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=88 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=513 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 555.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：前置時間=88 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=88 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=88 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=88 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b105-v14-31","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略下車階段會使僅按步速的撤離時間過度樂觀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting detraining makes a walking-speed-only evacuation estimate optimistic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"演練資料分列通知、下車、集結和步行階段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate notification, detraining, assembly and walking in exercise records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b105-v14-32","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略下車階段會使僅按步速的撤離時間過度樂觀。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting detraining makes a walking-speed-only evacuation estimate optimistic. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略下車階段會使僅按步速的撤離時間過度樂觀。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Omitting detraining makes a walking-speed-only evacuation estimate optimistic. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","忽略下車階段會使僅按步速的撤離時間過度樂觀。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Omitting detraining makes a walking-speed-only evacuation estimate optimistic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略下車階段會使僅按步速的撤離時間過度樂觀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting detraining makes a walking-speed-only evacuation estimate optimistic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b105-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b105-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"切內里系統交付情境中，兩組供電或控制設備若共用冷卻與通訊，須分開分析表面冗餘和共同故障。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For system handover, distinguish nominal redundancy from shared cooling and communications that can disable both power or control paths. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.014 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.014 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"切內里系統交付情境中，兩組供電或控制設備若共用冷卻與通訊，須分開分析表面冗餘和共同故障。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"For system handover, distinguish nominal redundancy from shared cooling and communications that can disable both power or control paths. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["切內里系統交付情境中，兩組供電或控制設備若共用冷卻與通訊，須分開分析表面冗餘和共同故障。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["For system handover, distinguish nominal redundancy from shared cooling and communications that can disable both power or control paths.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"切內里系統交付情境中，兩組供電或控制設備若共用冷卻與通訊，須分開分析表面冗餘和共同故障。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For system handover, distinguish nominal redundancy from shared cooling and communications that can disable both power or control paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b105-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.014 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000196 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00023716 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.014 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000196 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00023716 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.014 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000196 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00023716 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.014 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000196 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00023716 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.014 無因次。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.014 dimensionless.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.014 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.014 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b105-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：兩套主機同置一個失效環境不符合獨立失效率乘積假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two units exposed to one failing environment violate the independent-failure product assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿供電及通訊拓樸逐點追查共用設備和切換紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace shared equipment and transfer records along power and communications topology. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b105-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩套主機同置一個失效環境不符合獨立失效率乘積假設。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two units exposed to one failing environment violate the independent-failure product assumption. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩套主機同置一個失效環境不符合獨立失效率乘積假設。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Two units exposed to one failing environment violate the independent-failure product assumption. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩套主機同置一個失效環境不符合獨立失效率乘積假設。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Two units exposed to one failing environment violate the independent-failure product assumption.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩套主機同置一個失效環境不符合獨立失效率乘積假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two units exposed to one failing environment violate the independent-failure product assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b105-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響切內里基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ceneri Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鐵路通車需要土建、軌道、供電和控制的測試證據連結，研究切內里背景下的設備交付缺口。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Railway commissioning needs linked civil, track, power and control test evidence; examine gaps in a Ceneri-style handover. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=104 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=104 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"鐵路通車需要土建、軌道、供電和控制的測試證據連結，研究切內里背景下的設備交付缺口。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Railway commissioning needs linked civil, track, power and control test evidence; examine gaps in a Ceneri-style handover. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","鐵路通車需要土建、軌道、供電和控制的測試證據連結，研究切內里背景下的設備交付缺口。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Railway commissioning needs linked civil, track, power and control test evidence; examine gaps in a Ceneri-style handover.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鐵路通車需要土建、軌道、供電和控制的測試證據連結，研究切內里背景下的設備交付缺口。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Railway commissioning needs linked civil, track, power and control test evidence; examine gaps in a Ceneri-style handover. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b105-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=104 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.0769 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=104 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.0769 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=104 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.0769 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=104 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.0769 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：設備總數=104 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=104 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=104 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=104 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.6154 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b105-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：只有竣工圖而缺測試狀態，無法判斷設備是否已整合驗證。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: As-built drawings without test status do not establish integrated verification. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Ceneri Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從一個警報追到現場設備、測試程序和維修責任。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace one alarm to the field asset, test procedure and maintenance responsibility. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b105-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b105-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只有竣工圖而缺測試狀態，無法判斷設備是否已整合驗證。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"As-built drawings without test status do not establish integrated verification. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b105-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只有竣工圖而缺測試狀態，無法判斷設備是否已整合驗證。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"As-built drawings without test status do not establish integrated verification. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b105-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只有竣工圖而缺測試狀態，無法判斷設備是否已整合驗證。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","As-built drawings without test status do not establish integrated verification.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只有竣工圖而缺測試狀態，無法判斷設備是否已整合驗證。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"As-built drawings without test status do not establish integrated verification. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
